{"id": "unknown-2026-08-08-002", "date": "2026-08-08", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 32, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["improve", "decline"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "How US' Somnigroup's Q2 net income rose 12% despite sales decline?", "content": "Somnigroup’s Q2 FY26 net income rose 12 per cent to $110.9 million despite a 3 per cent sales decline to $1.82 billion, supported by margin expansion and higher operating income. \nGross margin improved to 44.8 per cent, while EBITDA rose to $280.8 million. \nThe company raised 2026 EPS guidance and focuses on Mattress Firm integration, the Stearns & Foster launch and Leggett & Platt acquisition.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/how-us-somnigroup-s-q2-net-income-rose-12-despite-sales-decline--312482-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
